From adf115833bd5bc3008e961274577dbf497e9deb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ChopGimp <mathieu.redon@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:17:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 104/106] ChopGimp: no more UI stalls on move / hide /
 Ctrl+click (alpha without babl reference conversion, cached Move controls)

Root cause (gdb sampling of the installed 3.25.0 on user-nofx.xcf):
- Move tool active: every undo step (layer drag release, eye click,
  Ctrl+click, Select > None, undo/redo) re-ran chopgimp_alpha_bounds()
  on the whole layer for the transform controls (chopgimp_move_refresh
  -> chopgimp_layer_content_bounds), ~300 ms on a 175 MB layer.
- That scan read the layer as "A u8": R'G'B'A u8 -> A u8 has no babl
  fast path, so babl_fish_reference_process_float() (slow, global mutex).
- Alpha to selection (gimp_channel_new_from_alpha) did the same
  conversion through a parallel gegl_buffer_copy(): all the GEGL
  workers and the main thread queued on babl_reference_mutex (~1 s of
  UI latency for ~0.3 s of main-thread CPU).

Fixes:
- chopgimp_alpha_bounds(): reads the buffer in its own format and tests
  the alpha component (RGBA/YA models, any precision), in parallel;
  old conversion path kept for other formats.
- chopgimp_alpha_bounds_cached(): result kept on the GeglBuffer until
  its "changed" signal; used only to draw the Move tool controls (crops
  still recompute).
- chopgimp_alpha_extract(): direct parallel copy of the alpha component,
  used by gimp_channel_new_from_alpha() (fallback: gimp_gegl_buffer_copy).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
